On Thu, Jan 15, 2009 at 9:42 AM, Alan Post <
terminal-keyword-lojban.416ddb@c0redump.org> wrote:

> [I appologize if you see this twice, I'm not certain it properly
> sent the first time.]
>
> I am reading through the level0 brochure, and I think I have
> gathered enough information to spell my first name (Alan) in
> lojban.
>
> Given that cmene cannot have the word "la" in it[1], and reading
> over the pronunciation guide[2], I think the closest spelling and
> pronunciation in Lojban of "Alan" is "Alyn.".
>

If you chose to go by the "Dot Side" proposal, {la} is permissable within
cmene, so you could be {.alan.}. Also, all words in Lojban are stressed
penultimately, i.e., on the second-to-last syllable, unless otherwise
indicated, usually by capitalizing the vowel of the syllable that should be
stressed.

>
> This accounts for the stress of the first syllable instead of the
> last, and sounds about right when I pronounce it: "/AH,luhn/"
>
> How did I do?  Is there a closer approximation?
>
> Thank you!
>
> -Alyn.
